{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310663,"nonce":"zCtwXvMsvpoEq/C+yudt/SN8aB4=","title":"ALL PARTS FIXED 2026-09-05 (a,b,c,d,e — map values render by tag, Std.string via toString, Null\u003cBool\u003e box, Null\u003cString\u003e members, anon ...","message":"**(a) `Null\u003cString\u003e` members** — repro `$SP/nullstr`: `var w:Null\u003cString\u003e = \"hello\"; w.length` → 0,\n`w.charAt(1)` → `\u003cunknown type …\u003e`; `f(s:Null\u003cString\u003e) return s == null ? -1 : s.length` → `f(\"abc\")`=0.\n`convert_type(Optional{String})` = String (raw pointer) — representation is right; the receiver\npaths (`lower_field_access` :515 and `try_extern_class_method_call` :48) call\n`resolve_through_aliases`, which had no `Optional` arm, so the String property/method mapping\n(`map_method!(instance \"String\", \"length\" …)`) was never selected. Fix: Optional-of-reference\n(String/Class/Interface/Array/Anonymous/Function/Enum/Map/TypeAlias) resolves to the inner type;\nscalar `Null\u003cInt\u003e` stays a box.\n\n**(d) anon field named like a class property (Issue12700's real cause)** — `lower_field_access`\nfalls back to a NAME-based scan of `property_access_map` when the field symbol is not a known\nproperty; with an `Anonymous` receiver `receiver_type_class_name` is None so the owner filter is\nskipped and `StringBuf.length`/`haxe.io.BytesBuffer.length` (both `(get, never)`) match ⇒ the anon\npointer is passed to `get_length` ⇒ garbage (`-48806491`, or a denormal float printed as\n`0.000…` — the recorded \"flake\"). The reference binary at 721e10d0 printed 0.5 for the same probe:\nthe fallback fires or not depending on symbol/iteration ORDER, which is why the corpus row was\nbistable. FIX: skip the name-based fallback for `Anonymous` receivers. Repros `$SP/i12700_read`\n(`var o = {time: 1.0, length: 0.5}; o.length`), `$SP/i12700_direct`, `$SP/i12700`.\nLESSON: a corpus row that flips between PASS and a garbage-looking value is an UNINITIALISED READ\nwhose visibility depends on ordering, not a nondeterministic runtime — reproduce it standalone.\n\n**(e) Issue12700's SECOND root (after the anon guard the row read `1 != 1`)** — harness form only:\n`class Issue12700 extends Test { eq(1.0, notes[0].length) }` → inherited `Test.eq\u003cT\u003e(v:T, v2:T)`\n→ `Assert.equals(v, v2)` with `Dynamic` formals. The template passed the erased RAW BITS straight\nthrough (`call equals($1: i64, $2: i64, null)` — no box), so `expected != actual` compared the f64\nbits of 1.0 as pointers. The ref binary printed NOTHING for the same replica (pre-existing).\nReplica: `$SP/hf12700` (Test.hx + Assert.hx shim + rayzor.toml; run `rayzor run --release --no-cache`\nfrom the dir — multi-file needs the manifest). Fix in flight: `maybe_box_value_inner` boxes a\nTypeParameter-typed value for a Dynamic formal via `haxe_box_value_by_tag(bits, tag)` with a\n`type_param_tag_fixups` placeholder (the same mechanism `haxe_value_to_string_by_tag` uses);\ndepends on the monomorphizer specializing the inherited generic method (verify: output ok/ok/ok).\n\n**(b) map formatting** — runtime `haxe_{string,int,object}map_to_string` cannot know V: values\nprint as the raw u64 (`[1 =\u003e 36506716128]` for a String value) and `Std.string(map)` on a\n`Map\u003cInt,String\u003e` literal prints `\u003cunknown type N\u003e`. The direct call site knows V statically —\na per-kind variant (as the `get` adapters do) is the shape of the fix. Braces → brackets landed.\n\n**(c) Bool values — DIAGNOSED + FIXED 2026-09-05, see [[bugs-loop-body-conditional-update-and-exit-phi]]: not a conversion bug at all, the CONDITIONAL INCREMENT in the loop body was lost. `m.get(\"a\")` printing `1` for a `Null\u003cBool\u003e` remains open (the box prints as int).** Was: — `for (x in m.iterator()) if (x)` over `StringMap\u003cBool\u003e` counts 0 while\n`for (x in m)` counts 1: the handle path's element conversion for Bool differs from the values-array\npath. `\"get=\" + m.get(\"a\")` prints `1` (Null\u003cBool\u003e box printed as int). Repro `$SP/vk_bool_direct`.\n\nSee [[bugs-erased-null-t-box-at-type-param-boundary]], [[bugs-imap-never-loads-generic-subtype-import]].\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): FIXED: `Null\u003cString\u003e` members (Optional-of-reference alias arm) + anon `{length:..}.length` ran `StringBuf.get_length` by BARE-NAME property fallback = Issue12700's real 'flake' (garbage read, order-dependent). OPEN: map toString prints non-Int VALUES as raw u64, `Std.string(map)`=\u003cunknown type\u003e; StringMap\u003cBool\u003e iterator yields false.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_null_reference_receivers_and_map_formatting` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}